{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734658",
      "title": "CSS Styling & CSS Modules",
      "sourceHash": "c9127060c3bd2086fb7a1dfb552d96eea1b33502053a611a0564d1ecf4663009",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "So we got a reusable component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "but one thing's missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "I guess a lot of things are still missing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.87,
          "en": "but one thing that's missing on our component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 14.52,
          "en": "is some styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.52,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "We have some white text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 17.741,
          "en": "and right now it's not even easy to tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.741,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "where one component ends and the next one begins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "I mean, we know because we created it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "This name is the start of the second time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "we're using this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "of the second component instance, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "but it's not obvious to see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "And in general, typically you wanna style your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "and not just at the markup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 44.18,
          "en": "Just as for any website, you don't just want the HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 46.113,
          "en": "you instead also want styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "Now for React, there is an endless amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "of styling solutions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 54.54,
          "en": "and I talk more about different approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "for styling components in my complete guide course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "You can for example, add inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "by adding the style attribute to your elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "Now here, the important thing to understand though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "is that you should not add your styles like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 74.37,
          "en": "So some string, some text that defines your styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 77.37,
          "en": "but that instead you should add a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.37,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "and then pass a JavaScript object as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "So this is not some special double curly braces syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 88.71000000000001,
          "en": "instead it's still the same single curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "syntax we used down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 95.85,
          "en": "but with the object passed as a value to the style prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 98.75999999999999,
          "en": "And then in that object you set your styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.75999999999999,
          "end": 103.35,
          "en": "like for example, color red and text aligned left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.35,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "if you would want to make it really ugly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 111.42,
          "en": "With that code, we would get that styling and yeah...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.42,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "But that's one way of styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 117.53999999999999,
          "en": "but just as with vanilla HTML and CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.53999999999999,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "typically you don't wanna use inline styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "Instead, it's considered better practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "to put your CSS code into CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 132.66,
          "en": "And indeed this project has one CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.66,
          "end": 135.153,
          "en": "with some styles being predefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "And what you could do is add a class to your div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.85,
          "en": "and then for example, give this a class of post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 147.75,
          "en": "to then set the appropriate styles in index.css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.75,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "But wait a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 154.07,
          "en": "did I just write className here instead of class?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 155.64,
          "en": "Yes, I did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.64,
          "end": 160.32,
          "en": "The JSX code you write might look like HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 163.41,
          "en": "but it actually isn't HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "Instead it is a JavaScript version of HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 171.51,
          "en": "and some HTML attributes have different names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.51,
          "end": 175.74,
          "en": "Now, to be honest, not too many, so nothing to worry about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.74,
          "end": 178.92000000000002,
          "en": "But class is one of the most important attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.92000000000002,
          "end": 182.4,
          "en": "that has a different name when writing JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 186.09,
          "en": "Instead of assigning CSS classes with the class attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.09,
          "end": 187.983,
          "en": "you instead use className.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.48,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "Now there are some technical reasons for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "that the JavaScript elements that are created under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "have className as a property name for setting CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 203.763,
          "en": "but those details aren't too important too keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.69,
          "end": 207.18,
          "en": "Instead, what is important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.18,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "is that CSS className are added to elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 215.84,
          "en": "with the className prop and not with just class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.39,
          "end": 218.28,
          "en": "But with that name being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 221.37,
          "en": "you can then set any className of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 223.05,
          "en": "And if we use post here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "we could for example add a post class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "in the index.css file to give this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 231.753,
          "en": "a background color of light blue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "And if we do that, we would see that background color here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 238.47,
          "en": "Obviously still ugly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.47,
          "end": 241.56,
          "en": "but that's another approach for assigning styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.56,
          "end": 244.256,
          "en": "We can set up global CSS classes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.256,
          "end": 248.01,
          "en": "and assign their classNames like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 251.61,
          "en": "But besides the fact that this is rather ugly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.61,
          "end": 254.82,
          "en": "which of course is a problem that could be solved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.82,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "there is another problem related to this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "When using global classNames",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 262.8,
          "en": "you could have name clashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 266.069,
          "en": "in bigger, more complex projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.069,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "You could have multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 271.68,
          "en": "that use the post className internally, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.68,
          "end": 274.20799999999997,
          "en": "and your globally defined CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.20799999999997,
          "end": 276.813,
          "en": "could then clash with each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "Put in other words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 282.784,
          "en": "you might prefer to scope CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.784,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "to your different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "so that styles applied to the post component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 293.28,
          "en": "really only affect that component and can't possibly clash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.28,
          "end": 296.58,
          "en": "with other styles in other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.58,
          "end": 301.58,
          "en": "And React projects created with Create React App or Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "also support a solution for that problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 309.15,
          "en": "Instead of defining the post style like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.15,
          "end": 312.84,
          "en": "you can add a dedicated CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 315.9,
          "en": "which I'll name Post.module.css,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.9,
          "end": 320.31,
          "en": "which should typically be located next to the JSX file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.31,
          "end": 322.11,
          "en": "though it's not technically required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.11,
          "end": 323.463,
          "en": "it's just a convention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 326.67,
          "en": "What is technically required though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.67,
          "end": 330.51,
          "en": "is that the file name is Post.module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.51,
          "end": 333.27,
          "en": "and then .css the extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.27,
          "end": 335.733,
          "en": "but the .module part is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 340.29,
          "en": "This tells Vite or Create React App",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.29,
          "end": 344.97,
          "en": "that you wanna use a feature called CSS modules here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 349.71,
          "en": "Now CSS modules is in the end an approach, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 349.71,
          "end": 352.8,
          "en": "an approach that's implemented by projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.8,
          "end": 356.25,
          "en": "created with Vite or Create React App",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.25,
          "end": 361.25,
          "en": "where the classNames you set in your CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 361.35,
          "end": 365.58,
          "en": "and which you then use in your HTML or JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 365.58,
          "end": 368.58,
          "en": "are under the hood transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 368.58,
          "end": 372.57,
          "en": "to guaranteed unique classNames",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 372.57,
          "end": 375.003,
          "en": "so that name clashes are avoided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 376.77,
          "end": 380.67,
          "en": "And by using .module in the CSS file name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 380.67,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "you tell Vite or Create React App",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 387.24,
          "en": "that you want to use this CSS modules feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 387.24,
          "end": 390.96,
          "en": "Now for this post component I prepared some styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 390.96,
          "end": 392.55,
          "en": "which you'll find attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 392.55,
          "end": 396.45,
          "en": "and I just pasted them into this Post.module.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 396.45,
          "end": 397.9,
          "en": "these attached styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 399.12,
          "end": 403.14,
          "en": "and we can now use them by going back to Post.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 403.14,
          "end": 405.15,
          "en": "and in there we now first of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 405.15,
          "end": 408.51,
          "en": "have to import this CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 408.51,
          "end": 412.86,
          "en": "Now in main.jsx, a CSS file is imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 412.86,
          "end": 415.05,
          "en": "by simply using the import keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.05,
          "end": 417.663,
          "en": "and then the path to the CSS file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 418.77,
          "end": 423.77,
          "en": "When using CSS modules this syntax must change a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 424.23,
          "end": 427.59,
          "en": "We do still import from that path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 427.59,
          "end": 430.95,
          "en": "so in this case from Post.module.css,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 430.95,
          "end": 433.98,
          "en": "which is the relative path to that CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 433.98,
          "end": 436.89300000000003,
          "en": "seen from that Post.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 437.94,
          "end": 440.76,
          "en": "But instead of just importing the file like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 440.76,
          "end": 445.76,
          "en": "we import classes or styles, the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 445.95,
          "end": 450.95,
          "en": "from that file so you must use this import syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
